Password & Credentials (REG-16): When submitting a bundle order, the local app transmits the student's password over HTTPS. Upon approval, the server hashes it (bcrypt) and stores it in Student.password_hash so recovery login after reinstall/lost phone works seamlessly.
Claiming After Manual Approval (REG-14):
The app generates a 256-bit random claimSecret and sends claimSecretHash = sha256(claimSecret) with the order.
The server stores claim_secret_hash with the pending order.
When Operations Admin approves the receipt, the server creates the student record, generates the MS number, and activates the entitlement.
The app (via polling or push notification) calls POST /orders/:orderId/claim with { claimSecret }.
The server validates sha256(claimSecret) === order.claim_secret_hash and returns { studentCode: "MS0001", token, refreshToken, entitlement }.
Takeover Protection on Linking (REG-11): If a submitted phone or email matches an existing paid student in the database, the order requires prior authentication (or OTP verification). Blind unauthenticated linking is rejected with ACCOUNT_EXISTS_LOGIN_REQUIRED.
Public Order Endpoint Hardening: Added rate limiting, strict receipt image validation (JPEG/PNG/WebP, size $\le$ MAX_RECEIPT_BYTES), and a cap of maximum 2 pending orders per phone number.
Local Data Migration (REG-12): When the claim endpoint returns the assigned MS number, the mobile app atomically updates local SQLite/SecureStore tables (progress, attempts, downloaded file mapping) from localAccountId to the server's MS0001 ID.
Gapless MS Counter: Using row-level locking on PostgreSQL (UPDATE counters SET value = value + 1 WHERE name = 'student_ms_code' RETURNING value;) inside the transaction to guarantee no skipped numbers.
Earlier Tests: Domain tests are written directly in Phase 1; counter, idempotency, and claim security tests in Phase 2.
